---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Chart from '../components/Chart.astro';
import { asset } from '../lib/paths';
import { monitored, verified, manualCost, ourCost } from '../data/series';
---

<Base>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" id="platform">
      <div class="col">
        <span class="logo" role="img" aria-label="Carbon Valinor" style={`--logo: url(${asset('logo.svg')})`}></span>
        <p data-words>
          <span class="lead" role="heading" aria-level="1">Carbon Valinor builds software for carbon.</span>{' '}
          Companies that capture and store CO₂ run long chains of equipment: capture
          units, compressors, pipelines, injection wells, and the rock underground. Our
          software connects to that equipment, models how each part behaves, and
          helps operators run the whole chain from one place.
        </p>
        <p data-words>
          We want storing carbon to be cheap to run and cheap to prove. Once it is,
          more of it will get done.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="monitoring">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Every tonne, accounted for.</span>{' '}
        We take in pressure readings from the wellhead and the bottom of the well,
        fibre-optic sensing along the wellbore, repeat seismic surveys, satellite
        measurements of ground movement and soil-gas samples. Reservoir simulations
        are updated as new data comes in, and statistical models learn what is normal
        for each site. Together they cover <span class="counter" data-keep>1,243,118</span>{' '}
        tonnes so far. When pressure drifts, the CO₂ spreads further than predicted or
        two meters disagree, the operator is told what changed and where. Every tonne
        is tracked from capture to injection, and every reading is stored with a
        timestamp in the formats regulators ask for.
      </p>
      <Chart
        id="stored"
        series={[
          { label: 'CO₂ monitored', value: '1.24 Mt', data: monitored },
          { label: 'Verified', value: '1.17 Mt', data: verified },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="cost">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Cheaper every year.</span>{' '}
        Proving that CO₂ stays underground costs money, and most of that cost is
        still people doing the work by hand. We automate the measurement, modelling
        and bookkeeping, so the cost per tonne drops every year without lowering the
        standard of proof.
      </p>
      <Chart
        id="cost"
        series={[
          { label: 'Manual, per tonne', value: '$18.40', data: manualCost },
          { label: 'With Carbon Valinor', value: '$4.20', data: ourCost },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="contact">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Work with us.</span>{' '}
        We work with operators across the CO₂ chain: capture, transport, storage and
        accounting. If you run any part of it, write to us.
      </p>
      <p class="closing" data-words>
        <a class="mail" href="mailto:info@carbonvalinor.com">info@carbonvalinor.com</a>
      </p>
      <footer><span data-words>© 2026 Carbon Valinor</span></footer>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
